postings.description:
The Hardware team at Hudson River Trading (HRT) creates high performance compute engines using FPGA and ASIC technologies to drive low latency trading decisions on global markets. We build custom solutions across the spectrum of speed and smarts: from bespoke circuits to world-class machine learning accelerators.&nbsp;
The FPGA/ASIC Design team and Verification team work in close collaboration, pushing boundaries in low-level computer architecture, logic design, tool writing, and the interface between hardware and software. There is often overlap in skills, and both teams work together very closely. The Hardware Engineering Summer 2027 Internship offers candidates the opportunity to explore both Design and Verification roles.
During HRT’s Hardware Engineering Internship, you will have the opportunity to create hardware in SystemVerilog (design) and build complex modeling and testing environments in Python (verification). You can always expect to be challenged by the ever-changing financial markets, and find yourself working on critical infrastructure in an extremely fast-paced, real-time environment.&nbsp;
What to Expect
A challenging and meaningful summer internship program that will give you an introduction to all technical facets of hardware engineering in the algorithmic trading industry&nbsp;
Independent projects that will have you deep dive into our hardware design and verification environments&nbsp;
An opportunity to work with and learn more about cutting edge FPGA/ASIC technology&nbsp;
After some intense but brief training, you’ll jump right into projects within your first two weeks of the program&nbsp;
You'll learn all about HRT's research and trading infrastructure, even in areas you won’t be working in
You’ll have the opportunity to learn about and gain a deeper understanding of the financial markets&nbsp;
Requirements
You are a full-time student in a Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering or related program
You will be graduating and looking for full-time roles in 2028
A thorough understanding of digital logic design and/or computer architecture&nbsp;
Experience using a hardware design language such as SystemVerilog
Familiarity with C++ and/or Python&nbsp;
Knowledge of Linux and familiar with its command prompt
A passion for technology and curiosity for how things work “under the hood”&nbsp;
Exceptional problem solving skills&nbsp;
Bonus: Familiarity with FPGAs or ASICs
Bonus: Exposure to a hardware verification flow such as UVM, or open-source verification tools such as cocotb
We do not allow multiple applications. Please apply to the ONE role you are most interested in and we will consider you for all open positions when reviewing your application.
Weekly base salary of 5,800 USD and a competitive signing bonus in addition to company-paid housing, meals, and other perks.
Culture
Hudson River Trading (HRT) brings a scientific approach to trading financial products. We have built one of the world's most sophisticated computing environments for research and development. Our researchers are at the forefront of innovation in the world of algorithmic trading.
At HRT we welcome a variety of expertise: mathematics and computer science, physics and engineering, media and tech. We’re a community of self-starters who are motivated by the excitement of being at the cutting edge of automation in every part of our organization—from trading, to business operations, to recruiting and beyond. We value openness and transparency, and celebrate great ideas from HRT veterans and new hires alike. At HRT we’re friends and colleagues – whether we are sharing a meal, playing the latest board game, or writing elegant code. We embrace a culture of togetherness that extends far beyond the walls of our office.
Feel like you belong at HRT? Our goal is to find the best people and bring them together to do great work in a place where everyone is valued. HRT is proud of our diverse staff; we have offices all over the globe and benefit from our varied and unique perspectives. HRT is an equal opportunity employer; so whoever you are we’d love to get to know you.
Please be advised: Use of AI tools by an applicant during interviews or assessments is strictly prohibited, unless otherwise instructed or agreed upon. We employ various methods to evaluate the authenticity of candidate responses. If we determine that AI assistance was used by an applicant during an interview or an assessment, we reserve the right to immediately end the interview or assessment, disqualify the applicant’s candidacy and/or rescind any job offers extended.
You can review our Global Applicant Privacy Notice , which explains how we process applicant information.
